{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1772835680195,"sessionID":"ses_33ac26176ffelh8nPkqSWau9bG","part":{"id":"prt_cc53daf930018Q78pNzMq5taHz","sessionID":"ses_33ac26176ffelh8nPkqSWau9bG","messageID":"msg_cc53da110001IcjSqtCeYibiFa","type":"tool","callID":"call_function_5kir2yrilewy_1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/paule/MAD/.tmp/webui-key-prompt.instructions"},"output":"<path>/home/paule/MAD/.tmp/webui-key-prompt.instructions</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: You are a senior software architect reviewing a feature plan.\n2: \n3: ## Feature: webui key prompt\n4: \n5: ### Original Description:\n6: The frontend should display a modal overlay prompting for the API key to allow access to the webui. The key is stored in localStorage for persistence. Without a valid key (either entered or stored), the backend should not send any actual data to the frontend - all content is blocked until authenticated.\n7: \n8: ### Generated Plan:\n9: I'll explore the codebase to understand the current implementation and create a comprehensive plan that addresses all the issues raised in the review feedback.\n10: Now let me check the template structure in index.html:\n11: Now I have a complete understanding of the codebase. Let me create a comprehensive plan that addresses all the issues identified in the review feedback.\n12: \n13: ```json\n14: {\n15:   \"questions\": [],\n16:   \"plan\": \"# WebUI Key Authentication Implementation Plan\\n\\n## Overview\\nImplement a modal overlay prompting for the dashboard key, stored in localStorage. Without a valid key, the backend must not send any actual data to the frontend.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 1: Fix Critical Modal Rendering Bug\\n\\n**Issue**: The key modal (index.html lines 250-257) is INSIDE the `{{if .Authenticated}}` block (line 210). Unauthenticated users see a blank page.\\n\\n**Solution**:\\n1. Restructure index.html to move key modal outside the `{{if .Authenticated}}` block\\n2. Add a separate `{{if .ShowKeyModal}}` or unconditionally render the modal container\\n3. Use JavaScript to show/hide the modal based on auth state\\n\\n**Implementation**:\\n- Move modal HTML to appear BEFORE the `{{if .Authenticated}}` conditional in index.html\\n- Keep modal in its own conditional that evaluates independently of authenticated state\\n- Backend passes `DashboardKeyConfigured` boolean to template (not just `Authenticated`)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 2: Fix Data Leakage - Server-Side Auth Enforcement\\n\\n**Issue**: api.go:139-153 fetches ALL clients/features before checking auth. Data is sent to browser but hidden with CSS.\\n\\n**Solution**:\\n1. Modify the root handler (api.go:125-159) to check authentication BEFORE fetching data\\n2. If not authenticated, render minimal page with modal but NO client/feature data\\n3. Return appropriate HTTP status (401) for API calls without valid key\\n\\n**Implementation**:\\n```go\\n// In registerRoutes, for \"/\" handler (api.go:125-159)\\nkey := r.URL.Query().Get(\\\"key\\\")\\nauthenticated := key != \\\"\\\" && (cfg.DashboardKey == \\\"\\\" || key == cfg.DashboardKey)\\n\\nif !authenticated {\\n    // Only render modal, no data\\n    data := map[string]interface{}{\\n        \\\"Key\\\":           \\\"\\\",\\n        \\\"Authenticated\\\": false,\\n        \\\"ShowKeyModal\\\":  cfg.DashboardKey != \\\"\\\", // Always show modal when key is required\\n        \\\"Clients\\\":       []Client{}, // Empty data\\n        \\\"StageGroups\\\":   []... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n17: }\n18: ```\n19: \n20: \n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## Your Task\n25: \n26: Review the plan and provide feedback. Consider:\n27: \n28: 1. **Completeness**: Does the plan cover all necessary aspects of the feature?\n29: 2. **Clarity**: Is the plan clear and unambiguous?\n30: 3. **Feasibility**: Are there any technical concerns or blockers?\n31: 4. **Edge cases**: What happens with edge cases or error conditions?\n32: 5. **Dependencies**: Are all dependencies identified?\n33: \n34: If previous feedback was provided, verify that the plan addresses those concerns.\n35: \n36: ## Output Format\n37: \n38: Respond with EXACTLY this format (no other text). Use PLAIN TEXT only:\n39: \n40: **VERDICT: PASS** or **VERDICT: FAIL**\n41: \n42: If FAIL, provide specific feedback:\n43: FEEDBACK: List each concern with what needs to be fixed or improved.\n44: \n45: Example:\n46: ```\n47: VERDICT: FAIL\n48: FEEDBACK:\n49: - Missing handling for network errors\n50: - Need to clarify data migration strategy\n51: - Consider adding rate limiting\n52: ```\n\n(End of file - total 52 lines)\n</content>","title":".tmp/webui-key-prompt.instructions","metadata":{"preview":"You are a senior software architect reviewing a feature plan.\n\n## Feature: webui key prompt\n\n### Original Description:\nThe frontend should display a modal overlay prompting for the API key to allow access to the webui. The key is stored in localStorage for persistence. Without a valid key (either entered or stored), the backend should not send any actual data to the frontend - all content is blocked until authenticated.\n\n### Generated Plan:\nI'll explore the codebase to understand the current implementation and create a comprehensive plan that addresses all the issues raised in the review feedback.\nNow let me check the template structure in index.html:\nNow I have a complete understanding of the codebase. Let me create a comprehensive plan that addresses all the issues identified in the review feedback.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"questions\": [],\n  \"plan\": \"# WebUI Key Authentication Implementation Plan\\n\\n## Overview\\nImplement a modal overlay prompting for the dashboard key, stored in localStorage. Without a valid key, the backend must not send any actual data to the frontend.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 1: Fix Critical Modal Rendering Bug\\n\\n**Issue**: The key modal (index.html lines 250-257) is INSIDE the `{{if .Authenticated}}` block (line 210). Unauthenticated users see a blank page.\\n\\n**Solution**:\\n1. Restructure index.html to move key modal outside the `{{if .Authenticated}}` block\\n2. Add a separate `{{if .ShowKeyModal}}` or unconditionally render the modal container\\n3. Use JavaScript to show/hide the modal based on auth state\\n\\n**Implementation**:\\n- Move modal HTML to appear BEFORE the `{{if .Authenticated}}` conditional in index.html\\n- Keep modal in its own conditional that evaluates independently of authenticated state\\n- Backend passes `DashboardKeyConfigured` boolean to template (not just `Authenticated`)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 2: Fix Data Leakage - Server-Side Auth Enforcement\\n\\n**Issue**: api.go:139-153 fetches ALL clients/features before checking auth. Data is sent to browser but hidden with CSS.\\n\\n**Solution**:\\n1. Modify the root handler (api.go:125-159) to check authentication BEFORE fetching data\\n2. If not authenticated, render minimal page with modal but NO client/feature data\\n3. Return appropriate HTTP status (401) for API calls without valid key\\n\\n**Implementation**:\\n```go\\n// In registerRoutes, for \"/\" handler (api.go:125-159)\\nkey := r.URL.Query().Get(\\\"key\\\")\\nauthenticated := key != \\\"\\\" && (cfg.DashboardKey == \\\"\\\" || key == cfg.DashboardKey)\\n\\nif !authenticated {\\n    // Only render modal, no data\\n    data := map[string]interface{}{\\n        \\\"Key\\\":           \\\"\\\",\\n        \\\"Authenticated\\\": false,\\n        \\\"ShowKeyModal\\\":  cfg.DashboardKey != \\\"\\\", // Always show modal when key is required\\n        \\\"Clients\\\":       []Client{}, // Empty data\\n        \\\"StageGroups\\\":   []... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n}\n```\n\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1772835680182,"end":1772835680194}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The user wants me to read a file with instructions and follow them exactly. Let me read the file first.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":"54721351261e7eadb55108cfbd7000471780e501e10b4c51ae16a73ac0de5416"}]}}}}
